 Candidate checks consist of complete frozen-input hashing, syntax/AST/source-view checks, and seven focused negative-control tests for the explicit base, dirty/wrong HEAD, external output paths, competing queue paths, unsafe artifact paths, script-closure corruption, and the full migration validation chain. These are script-preparation results only. Actual catalog generation, scope checks, Lean builds, benchmark tests and global results remain pending and must be recorded from future runs. `finalize.py` retains every attempt, including failures, and preserves the expected global completeness failure for 172 scopes. It does not infer current comparator or native numerical success.
 
 See `PLAN.md` for the exact future sequence. Review `evidence/lint-final/source-views.json`, the transformed files in that directory, and `evidence/final-checks.json`. Existing prior-script source files are preserved under `evidence/design-origin/`; they are design history only and are not executed by this candidate.
+
+## Revision 2 staging boundary
+
+Revision 1 and its independent counterexample remain frozen separately. The old stage gathered every current checkpoint file, so a file added after final validation could enter staging without belonging to the validation seal. Revision 2 requires exact equality with the sealed checkpoint paths plus `validation.json` before staging, permits only the newly created `staging-review.json` afterward, and uses `--no-renames` for literal path-set comparisons. No source integration, validation command, numerical predicate, protected pin, dependency, required build or expected count changes.
+
+Staging does not auto-reset or roll back. Failure after `git add` may retain index changes; a direct retry is blocked until root reviews an explicit repair. Existing staging reviews are retained and block duplicate execution. The focused stage controls use fresh `/tmp` files and in-memory Git simulations only; they never run a Git mutation or claim actual source acceptance.
